  "id": "autonomic-learning",
  "term": "autonomic learning",
  "definition": "Autonomic learning is an evolutionarily conserved form of functional Pavlovian conditioning proposed to occur in the autonomic nervous system. In this account, it develops between mother and fetus during gestation and continues after birth, shaping conditioned autonomic socioemotional reflexes that influence physiology and behavior.",
